g95-fu-computer-observe wiring (two edits in mixdog-tools/src/desktop/computer_act.rs and computer_feedback.rs, neither owned by this task)

1. computer_act.rs, fn preflight (anchor: `async fn preflight(&self, planned: &[Map<String, Value>], window_id: &str, cancel: &CancellationToken)`).
   Insert as the first statement of the body, before `let native: Vec<Value> = planned`:

       // The renderer's key table refuses a key it cannot map; a sequence found to hold one runs none of its steps (`electronKeyPresses` in `createInputPreflight`).
       for step in planned.iter().filter(|step| text(step, "action") == "key") {
           if let Some(refused) = APP_OWNED.unmapped_key(step, window_id) {
               return Ok(Some(refused));
           }
       }

   `AppOwnedWindows::unmapped_key` (computer_app_owned.rs) is new and has no other caller; until this is applied it only warns as dead code (the workspace does not deny warnings).
   The refusal is `background_unsupported: key {NAME} has no Electron input mapping; no input was sent`, a code `preflight` already turns into the sequence's refusal row.

2. computer_feedback.rs, fn serve (anchor: the line `let _ = mixdog_rt::time::timeout(SEND_TIMEOUT, desktop.request(HostCapability::Computer, Method(METHOD), params)).await;`).
   Replace it with:

       // A relay the desktop could not carry means the overlay surface that draws the arrow is gone: the next pointer action asks for the arrow again.
       if !matches!(mixdog_rt::time::timeout(SEND_TIMEOUT, desktop.request(HostCapability::Computer, Method(METHOD), params)).await, Ok(Ok(_))) {
           super::computer_pointer::forget_ready(&session);
       }

   `computer_pointer::forget_ready` is now `pub(super)` (this task).

No protocol rows, no Cargo edges, no SERVICE_PENDING names.
